  "engineering_rationale": {
    "clean_per_limit": "A provisional engineering receiver should completely and correctly deliver at least 90 percent of clean messages; therefore PER <= 0.10 replaces the invalidated v3 value 0.50. With 40 independently seeded clean messages, zero errors gives a two-sided Wilson 95 percent upper bound of approximately 0.0876, sufficient to test rather than merely observe this target.",
    "ebn0_gate": "Eb/N0=30 dB maps exactly to active-sample SNR=10 dB because Fs/Rb=100. This retains the physical noise point used by the invalidated v3 gate while correcting units and calibration.",
    "allocation": "Actual per-node allocation high-water is reported. No byte threshold is invented; missing channelizer or detector allocation diagnostics is machine FAIL.",
    "execution_budget": "The 64-channel CPU receiver creates substantial scheduling oversubscription. v5 observed a successful 26.583-second case and sporadic failures at the 30-second executor budget even when validation reproductions completed in 12.55 to 12.90 seconds. v6 freezes a 120-second executor budget and 150-second process guard; elapsed time remains reported and any timeout or noncompletion remains machine FAIL.",
    "v7_retry_basis": "The sealed v6 run remains FAIL because cochannel_fhss_sir_12_t6500 seed 38101 exceeded the 150-second process guard with no summary. Post-run diagnosis found O(samples*taps) front-erasure in each of 64 channelizer FIR histories. The circular-history replacement preserves exact convolution order and output bytes while making insertion work linear. Validation-only serial and two-way concurrent reproductions completed; v7 therefore uses a wholly fresh held-out partition and does not rerun any v6 held-out seed.",
    "v7_immutable_history": "v5 and v6 profiles, evaluators, raw journals, and reports are retained unchanged as historical failed evaluations; v7 does not reinterpret them.",
    "v7_prefreeze_validation": "C++26 affected and full partitioned libdsp suites, the DSP example suite, Phase 3 Python and CTest suites, frozen-report verification, JSON checks, two-way validation-only stress, and git diff --check passed before freeze."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Engineering simulation only; no hardware, conducted, channel-emulator, OTA, regulatory, interoperability, or product qualification.",
    "Phase noise is a discrete Wiener engineering model, not a measured oscillator mask.",
    "Static Rayleigh/Rician coefficients and the finite time-varying sum-of-sinusoids option are engineering models, not a claimed deployment profile.",
    "Hardware-like impairments are synthetic and have no passing product gate.",
    "The 500 Msps complex input represents configured IQ offsets; RF frequencies are metadata only.",
    "CFO diagnostics and decoder confidence are characterized but not qualified or probability-calibrated."
  ]
}
